(6653706, 993075, 43463, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the blue! Very well done conceptually- great expression and composition of elements! I guess it is the hat along with the circular shape of the glass that invokes a little of the imagery of Magritte - only instead of the apple covering the face I see the magnifying glass used as a means of self introspection of the spoken word.</td>', 'Congrats on the blue! Very well done conceptually- great expression and composition of elements! I guess it is the hat along with the circular shape of the glass that invokes a little of the imagery of Magritte - only instead of the apple covering the face I see the magnifying glass used as a means of self introspection of the spoken word.', '2012-01-24 10:22:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6653709, 992911, 43463, '<td valign="top">Well done Cory! Now I know why you choose the spot where you were. The low angle and side view gave your DPC audience a feel for not just the performer and her act but the reactions of the crowd behind her. Kate had such a wonderfully expressive face and you captured the ''having fun'' aspect very well. Glad to see that a candid street shot did so well.</td>', 'Well done Cory! Now I know why you choose the spot where you were. The low angle and side view gave your DPC audience a feel for not just the performer and her act but the reactions of the crowd behind her. Kate had such a wonderfully expressive face and you captured the ''having fun'' aspect very well. Glad to see that a candid street shot did so well.', '2012-01-24 10:28:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6653714, 993026, 43463, '<td valign="top">Glad to see that another photo from the GTG did so well in this challenge. It is a very well composed shot Marko. I like your shot of this homeless man and his dog more than mine - reason being that you captured the receiving cup along side with the help sign, the man is looking up so that the viewer can more easily establish eye contact (you get the sense of actually being there to see him asking for help rather than in mine where it just feels you are just observing from afar), and the sepia processing is very well done to call even more attention to the subjects without the distraction of color.</td>', 'Glad to see that another photo from the GTG did so well in this challenge. It is a very well composed shot Marko. I like your shot of this homeless man and his dog more than mine - reason being that you captured the receiving cup along side with the help sign, the man is looking up so that the viewer can more easily establish eye contact (you get the sense of actually being there to see him asking for help rather than in mine where it just feels you are just observing from afar), and the sepia processing is very well done to call even more attention to the subjects without the distraction of color.', '2012-01-24 10:37:01.000000', NULL, 0),
